  "methodology_note": "This mixed-effects model accounts for within-epoch triplet correlations via per-epoch random offsets (alpha_j ~ N(0, sigma_epoch\u00b2)), preserving triplet-level measurement precision.  It replaces both the overconfident triplet-binning (which ignores correlations) and the overly conservative epoch-blocked analysis (which discards within-epoch inverse-variance weighting).  The likelihood-ratio test is exact for nested Gaussian models.  The 95% amplitude interval is from parametric Gaussian draws in (A_1, A_2) using the REML fixed-effect covariance (see amplitude_interval.generator), not from resampling residuals."
